  /* ── parenthesis, after "20(25)": the month set as one running line of figures that wraps like a
     sentence, a wider space closing each week. The time from today to your day is an aside:
     a parenthesis opens before the first of the two and closes after the other, hung in the
     space between figures so nothing reflows; the figures inside it are set heavier. An aside
     that began last month only closes here. Gone is pencil, to come is ink, today the accent,
     yours the italic. Pointing sketches pencil parentheses round a figure; choosing inks the
